<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26399" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lĕvāmentum</span></b> , i,
			n.
		1. levo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an alleviation, mitigation, consolation,
			comfort</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">miseriarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fin. 5, 19, 53</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">doloris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Ep. 8, 19</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sine levamento,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					4, 66</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tributi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. H.
					1, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nec aliud levamentum quam si certis sub legibus
					militia iniretur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. A.
					1, 17</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praestare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					30, 3, 8, § 23</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mihi illam rem fore levamento,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 12, 43, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
